2025-12-05 17:26:14 - Agent_20251205171838 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed CodeQL query 20251205165225 regarding callback registration without callable validation in aiosignal/__init__.py. Found 1 confirmed vulnerability at line 58 where self.append(func) is called without validating that func is actually callable. The Signal class inherits from FrozenList and uses inherited list methods without type validation. While type hints exist (Callable[[Unpack[_Ts]], Awaitable[_T]]), Python does not enforce these at runtime. Non-callable objects can be added via inherited methods and will cause runtime errors when send() attempts to invoke them with await receiver(*args, **kwargs). This is a type confusion vulnerability (CWE-20) with medium severity and high likelihood of exploitation through denial of service.
